From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandr Astrouski <astrouski@google.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: skip redundant SSID and WPA IE checks for partner links

In IEEE 802.11be MLO, the SSID and RSN/WPA IEs are carried in the outer
(Re)Association Request frame at the MLD level. Per-STA Profile
subelements for partner links do not duplicate outer SSID or WPA IEs.

Skip check_ssid() and WPA IE presence checks when parsing partner link
profiles that already have an established association link / wpa_sm.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -4629,7 +4629,7 @@ static int __check_assoc_ies(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
 #endif /* CONFIG_ENC_ASSOC */
 #endif /* CONFIG_SAE */
 
-	if (type != LINK_PARSE_RECONF) {
+	if (type != LINK_PARSE_RECONF && !sta->mld_assoc_sta) {
 		resp = check_ssid(hapd, sta, elems->ssid, elems->ssid_len);
 		if (resp != WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS)
 			goto out;
@@ -4813,7 +4813,7 @@ static int __check_assoc_ies(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
 		sta->flags |= WLAN_STA_MAYBE_WPS;
 	} else
 #endif /* CONFIG_WPS */
-	if (hapd->conf->wpa && wpa_ie == NULL) {
+	if (hapd->conf->wpa && wpa_ie == NULL && !assoc_wpa_sm) {
 		hostapd_logger(hapd, sta->addr, HOSTAPD_MODULE_IEEE80211,
 			       HOSTAPD_LEVEL_INFO,
 			       "No WPA/RSN IE in association request");
